WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Monday morning, let's get into Tesla's short time, episode 540.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.200
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.020
Today is July 13th, 2026.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.240
A new week and plenty happening with Tesla.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.020
Tesla's Fremont factory tear down signals the shift

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.020
from legacy vehicles to optimist production scale.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.040
Tesla has started dismantling Model S and X lines

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.860
at Fremont to install robot production cells.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.580
The move reallocates existing factory space

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.380
rather than adding new capacity.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.060
A shok Eluswami noted optimist now carries

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.700
the quality bar set by those legacy lines.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.740
This change marks a physical shift in factory priorities

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.780
from passenger vehicles to robotics.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.180
Further updates are expected

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.040
as the first robot production lines become visible.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.760
The next visible milestone will be the first production cells

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.640
operating in the converted area.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.560
With factory space now committed to robots,

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.640
the next hardware bottleneck is the inference chips

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:01.600
that will run them.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.320
Factory space is finite and every square meter devoted

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.940
to one product line is unavailable for another.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.400
Tesla's decision to dismantle Model S and X assembly

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.820
at Fremont therefore represents an explicit reallocation

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.340
of capital equipment and floor area toward optimists

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.480
rather than an incremental expansion.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.140
The move compresses the timeline for robot production

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.640
only if the freed capacity can be repurposed faster

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.660
than building new facilities elsewhere.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.580
The economic logic rests on utilization rates

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.620
where legacy vehicle lines that were already running

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.280
below optimal volume now carry higher fixed costs per unit.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.760
Converting that space avoids the larger outlay

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:49.300
of greenfield construction while the robot program

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.760
is still proving demand.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.300
If optimist volumes ramp more slowly than projected,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.820
however, the company will have surrendered

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.060
proven passenger vehicle capacity

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.660
without an immediate replacement revenue stream.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:05.100
This choice also affects supply chain sequencing

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.580
with parts and tooling previously flowing

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.620
to Model S and X production now available

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.460
for redirection or retirement.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.080
The net margin impact will depend

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.520
on how quickly optimist unit economics reached the point

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.640
where robot gross profit exceeds the foregone vehicle contribution.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.080
Samsung Foundry has finished setup work

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.260
for volume production of Tesla's AI5 chip.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.180
The Taylor Texas plant is scheduled to start operations

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.220
later this year.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.680
The chip is intended for autonomous driving inference

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.640
in future vehicles and robots.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.680
Production timing will determine how quickly

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.320
HW5 AI5 hardware can reach the fleet.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.140
Samsung confirmed it will manufacture Tesla's AI5 chip

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.160
for autonomous driving applications.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.680
The agreement covers production at the Taylor facility

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.180
once operations begin.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.940
This marks another step in Tesla's move

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.220
toward custom silicon for both vehicles and robots.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.240
Volume output will influence how quickly next generation

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.200
inference hardware reaches customers.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.060
A cyber cab prototype was observed on public roads

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.400
in Hampton, New Hampshire.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.780
The siding adds to evidence of testing activity outside Texas.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.420
It remains unclear whether the vehicle was operating

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.740
in supervised or unsupervised mode during the drive.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.520
Next data point to watch is whether additional states

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.820
report similar sightings in coming weeks.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.380
A Texas permit confirms Tesla is preparing

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.540
an autonomous cleaning robot to service its cyber cab

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.960
and robot taxi fleet.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.620
The system is designed to operate without human drivers

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:45.820
at dedicated hubs.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.240
This infrastructure step addresses

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.840
one operational requirement for scaling a driverless network.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.900
Deployment timing will depend on vehicle production

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.640
and regulatory approval.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.280
Tesla's profit per vehicle has declined sharply

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.460
and now sits near Toyota's levels

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.400
after earlier wide leads.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:08.200
The drop reflects pricing pressure and mixed shifts

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.720
rather than production issues.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.020
Gross margins on vehicles remain under scrutiny

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.880
as the company invests in robot taxi and optimist programs.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.720
Investors will look for margin stabilization signals

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.580
in the next quarterly report.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.200
Jeffree's analysts raised their Tesla price target

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.700
to $400 from $375 while keeping a hold rating.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.260
The move follows Tesla's Q2 delivery beat

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.180
of more than 15%.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.280
The firm credited the strong automotive quarter

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.140
for the adjustment.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:44.000
Listeners should watch the next earnings call for confirmation

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.440
on whether delivery momentum continues into Q3.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.620
Tesla captured 30% of all imported vehicle sales

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.400
in South Korea during June.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.640
The result came as the country's total imported vehicle sales

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.580
rose 37% to 38,059 units.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.080
Tesla has now exceeded 200,000 cumulative units sold

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.920
in the market over 10 years.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.020
The milestone highlights sustained demand

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.880
even as local competitors prepare responses.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.760
Tesla and Hyundai jointly criticized a proposed state EV tax

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.440
that would effectively have electric owners

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.340
subsidizing hybrid purchases.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.020
The company's called the structure perverse

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.060
because it reverses the intended incentive direction.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.360
Both firms argued the policy would slow EV adoption

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.480
without clear environmental benefit.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.960
Regulators in the affected state

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.440
have not yet responded to the joint statement.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.220
FSD supervised detected and avoided a deer

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.020
despite direct sunlight glare.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.320
The system processed the obstacle in real time

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.880
without driver intervention.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.180
This incident demonstrates continued improvement

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.200
in edge case handling under challenging visibility.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.800
Observers will track whether similar performance holds

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.560
in upcoming software releases.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:06.480
Thieves in Nevada removed 11 Tesla battery trailers

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.700
over several weeks, removing equipment valued

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.360
in the millions.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.240
The incidents targeted high value energy storage assets

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.420
rather than vehicles.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:18.580
Local authorities have not released details

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.620
on suspects or recovery efforts.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.640
The scale of the thefts raises questions

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.160
about physical security at storage sites.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.460
An Australian owner detailed daily use

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.600
of a model Y as a family hauler,

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.720
noting range, charging habits, and interior space.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.480
The review highlighted how the vehicle handles school runs

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.200
and weekend trips without major compromises.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.880
Real-world efficiency figures matched Tesla's claims

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.260
under mixed conditions.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.700
The account adds to the growing set

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.920
of long-term owner data from right-hand drive markets.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:57.700
An owner reported 2,500 miles in the base cyber truck AWD

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.720
and concluded the truck remains competitively priced

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.960
at $70,000.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:06.400
The review focused on build quality, utility features,

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.680
and daily drivability rather than performance claims.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:13.160
No major issues were noted in the initial period.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:17.060
Continued owner reports will show whether early impressions

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.560
hold at higher mileage.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:22.880
A customer reported that Tesla recalled one power wall unit

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.460
drained both batteries over several months

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.960
and ultimately offered to replace the pair.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.460
The sequence left the homeowner without full backup

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.420
capacity during the outage period.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.240
Tesla has not commented publicly on whether this reflects

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:38.840
a broader service policy.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.260
Affected owners will monitor whether similar cases

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.700
surface and other regions.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.460
Ben Shapiro publicly asked Tesla to develop an eight-seat SUV

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.980
or minivan to serve larger families.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.640
Elon Musk replied that the company is doing its best

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.460
on the request.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.920
The exchange highlights ongoing customer demand

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.920
for more seating options beyond current model Y

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.340
and X configurations.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:07.600
No timeline or confirmation of development has been provided.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:11.280
Investor Ross Gerber stated he prefers his cyber truck

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.780
to his Rivian for daily use, yet remains critical

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.420
of FSD performance.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:19.380
The comments separate hardware preference

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.440
from software capability in one owner's experience.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.320
Gerber's view reflects a split assessment

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:28.020
common among some early cyber truck buyers.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.100
Future FSD updates will determine

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.740
whether the software gap narrows for this group.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.740
A comparison test showed the model-wise

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.600
screen-centric interface outperforming vehicles

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:43.120
with up to 50 physical buttons in usability metrics.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.080
Tester's noted faster menu navigation

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.980
once drivers adapted to the layout.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.420
The result challenges assumptions

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.080
that physical controls are inherently superior for all tasks.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.380
Future interior designs from other makers

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.660
may incorporate similar screen density.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.740
Before we go, keep an eye on whether the next earnings call

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.660
confirms delivery momentum into the third quarter.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.540
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:18.840
TSLA closed at $407.76, up $1.21, 0.3%.

